The gate is src/engine/lib.parity.test.ts (in npm test): vanilla's
vendor/pointers.js at sync-base against lib.ts, for every state
variable and every players[key] of the four fixtures at both points
(48 dereferences; solc's "$" read as "~" first, as the page does):
identical regions (name, location, slot, offset, length) and identical
bytes read; and some expressions evaluate the same. Vanilla's bundle
at sync-base embeds the commit it was built from (d7cb421a3, the pin
before this one; the test checks it).

To re-pin: in a detached ethdebug/format worktree at the commit, yarn
install --frozen-lockfile; npm pack packages/format,
packages/pointers, packages/evm and packages/programs-react into
vendor/ (replace the .tgz); update this file (commit, sha256); drop
the @ethdebug entries from package-lock.json and
node_modules/@ethdebug, then npm install (else npm keeps the old
integrity); npm test (the parity gate). A running dev server restarts
and pre-bundles the library again when this file or the lockfile
changes (vite.config.ts repin; test/e2e/repin.spec.ts); without that,
its cache keeps the old library and the page fails ("failure to
recognize kind of expression").
